# Normalise line endings to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Roughly sixteen tests in tests/ assert against the raw text of source files
# (.tsx, .css, .rs, .md, .srt). Under git's default autocrlf on Windows those
# files check out with CRLF, and any assertion that anchors on "\n" stops
# matching — which is exactly how the tutorial SRT test failed on
# windows-latest while passing on macos-14.
#
# There are no .bat/.cmd/.ps1 files in this repo, so nothing needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary
*.dmg binary
*.exe binary
*.pdf binary
